osure most efficiently per dollar of notional? No, beta is linear. $1 of SOL short reduces beta exposure by $1.5. $1 of MATIC short reduces by $1.3. $1 of BTC short reduces by $1.0. So hedging SOL is most efficient for beta reduction. $180k SOL short reduces beta exposure by $180k * 1.5 = $270k. $220k MATIC short reduces beta exposure by $220k * 1.3 = $286k. Total Beta Reduction = $556k. Total Initial Beta Exposure = $1007.85k. 556 / 1007.85 = 55.1%. This meets the >50% requirement. So the strategy is valid. Worst case residual PnL: -$73.51k.",
